  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I did not run `vite build` or load the page in a browser, so the render itself is unchecked.\n\n- **Instancing:** the ground is one plane. Trunks (8,000) and canopies (8,000) are two instanced draws, and the 2,000 rocks are a third. That makes 10,000 objects, with each tree counted once.\n- **Determinism:** positions, scales and colours all come from one seeded LCG, so the forest is the same on every load. Objects are placed uniformly in a disk of radius 46.\n- **Colour variation:** each canopy, trunk and rock gets its own HSL colour per instance.\n- **Light and fog:** one shadow-casting directional light (\"sun\") with a 4096 shadow map fitted to the forest, plus exponential fog (`mode: \"exp\"`, density 0.006). I also added a neutral environment and a hemisphere light, which are fill light only.\n- **Camera:** it orbits at radius 100 and height 58 at about 0.12 rad/s, looking at the origin, so the whole forest stays in view. It moves through `app.camera.setPose` in `onFrame`.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` is set inside the first `onFrame` callback. I'm not certain the callback runs after the first frame is drawn rather than just before it.\n- **Shadow fit:** I read `extent: 60` as covering the forest, but I didn't confirm whether the engine treats it as a half-size or a full width.\n\n",
